---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CopyBlock from '../components/CopyBlock.astro';
import { toolFamilies, marketplace } from '../data/tools';
---

<Layout
  title="ExFu agent tools & setup"
  description="Explore ExFu plugins, add the marketplace and follow setup instructions for the tool you choose. Help for Cowork, Claude Code, ChatGPT and Codex users."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow red">ExFu agent tools</p><h1>
        Tools for agents.<br />Help getting started.
      </h1><p class="lead tools-lead">
        Explore the plugins, choose what would help, and get it working. Everything you need to
        start is below.
      </p><a class="button" href={marketplace} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Explore the full marketplace ↗</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap tools-layout">
    <nav class="tools-sidebar" aria-label="Tools page sections">
      <p class="eyebrow">On this page</p><a href="#tool-catalogue">Explore the tools</a><a
        href="#marketplace">1. Add the marketplace</a
      ><a href="#setup">2. Choose & install</a><a href="#first-session">3. First session</a><a
        href="#troubleshooting">Get unstuck</a
      >
    </nav>
    <div class="tools-main">
      <section id="tool-catalogue" class="tools-chapter">
        <p class="eyebrow red">Find your starting point</p><h2>What would help your agent?</h2><p>
          These are a few of the main plugins. The <a
            href={marketplace}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">marketplace</a
          > often has more tools and editions than we list here, along with their current documentation.
        </p><div class="tools-choices">
          {
            toolFamilies.map((tool) => (
              <article>
                <>
                  <h3>{tool.name}</h3>
                  <p>{tool.description}</p>
                  <a href="#setup" data-choose-plugin={tool.pkg} class="text-link">
                    Set up this plugin ↗
                  </a>
                </>
              </article>
            ))
          }<article class="more-tools">
            <h3>And more</h3><p>
              See what else is available, including other editions and new additions.
            </p><a class="text-link" href={marketplace} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Browse the marketplace ↗</a
            >
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="marketplace" class="tools-chapter">
        <p class="eyebrow red">Step 1 · Once per app</p><h2>Add the ExFu marketplace.</h2><p>
          The marketplace is the catalogue of ExFu plugins. Choose your app below to see how to
          access it, then choose whichever plugins you want. If you have already added it, <a
            href="#setup">go straight to your plugin</a
          >.
        </p>
        <fieldset class="app-picker" hidden>
          <legend>Which app are you using?</legend>
          <p id="app-choice-help">
            Choose once for the instructions below. You can switch at any time.
          </p>
          <div class="app-options">
            <label
              ><input
                type="radio"
                name="setup-app"
                value="cowork"
                checked
                aria-describedby="app-choice-help"
              /> Cowork</label
            >
            <label
              ><input
                type="radio"
                name="setup-app"
                value="code"
                aria-describedby="app-choice-help"
              /> Claude Code</label
            >
            <label
              ><input
                type="radio"
                name="setup-app"
                value="codex"
                aria-describedby="app-choice-help"
              /> Codex</label
            >
            <label
              ><input
                type="radio"
                name="setup-app"
                value="chatgpt"
                aria-describedby="app-choice-help"
              /> ChatGPT</label
            >
          </div>
          <p id="app-selection-status" role="status">Showing Cowork instructions.</p>
        </fieldset>
        <div class="setup-options">
          <article class="setup-option" data-setup-app="cowork">
            <h3>In Cowork</h3><p>
              In Claude Desktop, open Cowork, then <strong>Customize → Plugins</strong>. Under
              Personal plugins, choose <strong>+ → Add marketplace</strong> and add from a repository.
            </p><CopyBlock text={marketplace} label="Copy marketplace address" /><a
              href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13837440-use-plugins-in-claude"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude’s plugin guide ↗</a
            >
          </article><article class="setup-option" data-setup-app="code">
            <h3>In Claude Code</h3><p>
              With Claude Code installed and signed in, paste this into your terminal:
            </p><CopyBlock
              text="claude plugin marketplace add ExFu/exfu-marketplace"
              label="Copy terminal marketplace command"
            /><p>Or, inside a Claude Code conversation:</p><CopyBlock
              text="/plugin marketplace add ExFu/exfu-marketplace"
              label="Copy conversation marketplace command"
            /><a
              href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/discover-plugins"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude Code plugin guide ↗</a
            >
          </article>
          <article class="setup-option" data-setup-app="codex">
            <h3>In Codex</h3><p>
              With the Codex CLI installed, run this in your terminal to add the marketplace:
            </p>
            <CopyBlock
              text="codex plugin marketplace add ExFu/exfu-marketplace"
              label="Copy Codex marketplace command"
            />
            <p>
              Then install your chosen plugin in step 2. Use the same local account for the CLI and
              the Codex app.
            </p>
            <a
              href="https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI’s plugin guide ↗</a
            >
          </article>
          <article class="setup-option" data-setup-app="chatgpt">
            <h3>In ChatGPT</h3><p>
              Open <strong>Plugins</strong>, if available, and look for the ExFu plugin you want.
              Availability depends on your account and workspace. Apps connects services; it does
              not install this GitHub marketplace.
            </p>
            <p>
              In a managed workspace, ask your administrator about importing the ExFu marketplace
              from GitHub. A plugin marked <strong>Desktop only</strong> needs a supported desktop app.
            </p>
            <CopyBlock text={marketplace} label="Copy marketplace address for your administrator" />
            <a
              href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001256/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT plugin availability and setup ↗</a
            >
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="setup" class="tools-chapter plugin-workspace">
        <div class="plugin-picker" hidden>
          <p class="eyebrow red">Step 2 · Your chosen plugin</p><label for="plugin-choice"
            >What are we installing?</label
          ><select id="plugin-choice"
            >{toolFamilies.map((tool) => <option value={tool.pkg}>{tool.name}</option>)}</select
          ><p id="plugin-selection-status" role="status">Showing Agent Library instructions.</p>
          <p class="app-choice-reminder" hidden>
            Using <span data-current-app>Cowork</span>. <a href="#marketplace" data-change-app
              >Change app</a
            >
          </p>
        </div><div class="selected-plugin-body">
          <h2 id="selected-tool-title">Install the Agent Library.</h2><p
            id="selected-plugin-description"
          >
            {toolFamilies[0].detail}
          </p><p>Marketplace added? These instructions install just this plugin.</p><div
            class="setup-options"
          >
            <article class="setup-option" data-setup-app="cowork">
              <h3>In Cowork</h3><p>
                Browse your ExFu marketplace and find <strong data-selected-plugin-name
                  >exfu-agent-library-solo</strong
                >. Choose Install, then check that it is enabled.
              </p>
            </article><article class="setup-option" data-setup-app="code">
              <h3>In Claude Code</h3><p>In your terminal:</p><div id="selected-terminal">
                <CopyBlock
                  text="claude plugin install exfu-agent-library-solo@exfu-marketplace"
                  label="Copy Agent Library install command"
                />
              </div><p>Or in a Claude Code conversation:</p><CopyBlock
                text="/plugin install exfu-agent-library-solo@exfu-marketplace"
                id="selected-slash"
              />
            </article>
            <article class="setup-option" data-setup-app="codex">
              <h3>In Codex</h3><p>Install the selected plugin from your terminal:</p>
              <CopyBlock
                text="codex plugin add exfu-agent-library-solo@exfu-marketplace"
                id="selected-codex"
                label="Copy Codex plugin install command"
              />
              <p>
                Start a fresh local task in the Codex app or CLI and check that the plugin’s skills
                are available.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="setup-option" data-setup-app="chatgpt">
              <h3>In ChatGPT</h3><p>
                If <strong data-selected-plugin-name>exfu-agent-library-solo</strong> is available in
                your plugin directory, open it, review its requirements and choose <strong
                  >Install plugin</strong
                >. Connect any required apps when prompted.
              </p>
              <p>
                If it is unavailable, use the Projects starting point below or choose Codex for
                local plugin setup. A repository link in a chat does not install the plugin.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <section id="first-session" class="setup-next">
            <p class="eyebrow red">Step 3 · Try your chosen plugin</p><p>
              Start a fresh session in the app where the plugin is installed. Check that its skills
              are available before asking it to run setup.
            </p><div data-setup-app="cowork code codex">
              {
                toolFamilies.map((tool, i) => (
                  <div data-plugin-first={tool.pkg} hidden={i !== 0}>
                    <>
                      <h3>{tool.setupTitle}</h3>
                      <p>{tool.preparation}</p>
                      <p>Paste this to begin:</p>
                      <CopyBlock text={tool.setupPrompt} label={`Copy ${tool.name} setup prompt`} />
                      <p>{tool.setupNote}</p>
                    </>
                  </div>
                ))
              }
            </div>
            <div data-setup-app="chatgpt">
              <h3>Start with one useful task.</h3>
              <p>
                If installed, select the plugin with an @ mention or the + menu when available. Ask
                it which of its skills can run in this chat before starting.
              </p>
              <CopyBlock
                text="Check whether the selected ExFu plugin and its skills are available in this chat. Explain what can run here and any setup needed. Then help me try it on one real task."
                label="Copy ChatGPT plugin starting prompt"
              />
              <h3>If the plugin is not available</h3>
              <p>
                Create a ChatGPT Project for your work. Add relevant reference files and project
                instructions describing the outcome, your preferences and what you want to review.
                This gives you a place to continue the work; it does not run the ExFu plugin or its
                local automation.
              </p>
              <CopyBlock
                text="Help me set up this project around one recurring task. Ask what I want to achieve, which reference files will help and what I want to review myself. Then draft concise project instructions and help me try them on a small example."
                label="Copy ChatGPT Project starting prompt"
              />
              <a
                href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10169521-projects-in-chatgpt"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer">ChatGPT Projects guide ↗</a
              >
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="troubleshooting" class="tools-chapter">
        <p class="eyebrow red">A little support</p><h2>Something not working?</h2><article
          class="faq-answer"
        >
          <h3>I can’t find the plugin.</h3><p>
            Check that the ExFu marketplace was added in the app you are using, and the plugin is
            installed and enabled. On a managed work account, your administrator may need to allow
            it.
          </p>
        </article><article class="faq-answer">
          <h3>My app doesn’t recognise the setup.</h3><p>
            Start a new session in the app where you installed the plugin. Select your working
            folder and ask whether your agent can see the plugin’s skills. If not, restart the app
            and check your installed plugins.
          </p>
        </article><div class="tools-help">
          <h3>Still stuck?</h3><p>
            Email <a href="mailto:al@exfu.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >al@exfu.ai</a
            > with the app you’re using, the step you reached and the error message. Leave out passwords
            and private client information.
          </p><a class="text-link" href="/personal-support/">Prefer to get set up together? ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div><script src="../scripts/tool-setup.ts"></script></Layout
>
